<title>NETHERLANDS: Bangert cuts Heineken to Sell.</title>
<headline>Bangert cuts Heineken to Sell.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1996-09-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Summary of Sept 18 research.</p>
<p>Company---------Sector--------Price---Broker----------------</p>
<p>Heineken	  Brewers	 306.00  Bangert Pontier</p>
<p>COMMENT: Sell from Hold. Given Heineken's expectation double digit earnings growth will be difficult to maintain in medium term, Bangert thinks current valuation is very demanding...18 times 1998E earnings is fair as a prospective P/E ratio...which implies a fair price of 270 guilders.</p>
<p>    Estimates (Dfl):   EPS	pvs	P/E     Dividend</p>
<p>    1995 (actual)	13.23		 21.5    3.50</p>
<p>    1996		   12.70   (14.80)   24.1    3.50</p>
<p>    1997		   13.80   (16.45)   22.2    3.50</p>
